  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Embedded Generation Investment Programme (EGIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EGIP aims to support the pioneering development of a viable and alternative procurement mechanism, at scale, for renewable energy involving non-sovereign entities such as industries and municipalities.

&#x2022; The framework supports the development of new RE market modalities and business models by facilitating a disintermediation of RE markets through non-sovereign offtake
&#x2022; The framework also aims to promote an increased involvement and equity participation of local communities and South African MSMES, which mainstreams local communities and business with the country&#x2019;s climate targets and is aligned with the country&#x2019;s socio-economic objective of mainstreaming the majority black participation in the national economy.</narrative>
  </description>
